# --- 🧰 The Toolchain's Downloads ---
#
# Every tool install.sh downloads, one value per line, read by install.sh
# and by the tests. The Python tools are pinned in requirements.txt and the
# Node tools in package-lock.json, beside this file; the base image is
# pinned by digest in the Dockerfile.
#
# Each version started as the one the standards' checks ran when this
# repository took them over. They install these now, through
# .github/actions/toolchain, so a tool behaves in CI as it does in the image:
#
#   NODE        22.x, the Node.js line ci.yml sets up. The newest 22 release.
#   ACTIONLINT  The version lint-workflows.yml built, in the standards.
#   GITLEAKS    The version gitleaks-action installed for 🔍 Scan for Secrets.
#   TYPOS       The version of the typos action 📝 Check Spelling ran.
#   LYCHEE      The version the lychee action 🔗 Check Links ran installed.
#   SHELLCHECK  The newest release. actionlint called whichever the runner had.
#
# Each SHA-256 is of the release archive install.sh downloads for that
# architecture: AMD64 for linux/amd64, ARM64 for linux/arm64. Node's,
# actionlint's, gitleaks' and lychee's match the checksums their projects
# publish beside the archives. typos and shellcheck publish none, so theirs
# were taken from the archives GitHub served the day they were pinned.
#
# To move a tool, change its version and both of its sums in one commit, and
# run `make test`, which builds the image and checks every version it holds.

